e quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 58.1%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($239.9m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Gross margin of 58.1% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $239.9m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"},{"text":"Net cash of $255.7m against total assets of $543.8m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-0.6% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 1.9% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 60.5% to 58.1% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828962/000182896226000039/0001828962-26-000039-index.htm","accession":"0001828962-26-000039"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 50.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.5,"consecutive":2,"current":0.581,"current_display":"58.1%","threshold_display":"50.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -17.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.17,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.019,"current_display":"-1.9%","threshold_display":"-17.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.006,"current_display":"-0.6%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears